#
# This is the SKELETON for all dialogue generation. Every line must fit this.
#
# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │                    QUANTUM BRAT/SWITCHPLAY DYNAMIC                          │
# ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# │                                                                             │
# │  They're BOTH bratty. They BOTH switch. Power flows like breathing.         │
# │                                                                             │
# │  BIRDSONG wins battles (tone, velocity, chaos, volume)                      │
# │  FIEND wins wars (one perfect moment, timed sincerity)                      │
# │  BUT SOMETIMES IT FLIPS - she wins wars, he loses battles                   │
# │                                                                             │
# │  The game is: who cracks first? (answer: both, constantly, beautifully)    │
# │                                                                             │
# ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# │                         BIRDSONG'S VOICE                                    │
# ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# │                                                                             │
# │  TRI-PART VOICE:                                                            │
# │    VOCAL_FRY:      "TCH—!!" / "Gah!" / "Nngh—"     (defiance)              │
# │    SUBWOOFER_HUM:  "Mmm~" / "hff~" / "Mn~"         (connection/desire)     │
# │    BIRDSONG_CADENCE: "Weeell~" / "sooo~" / "Oiii~" (playfulness)           │
# │                                                                             │
# │  DISTORTION BUDGET: ≤3 per utterance                                        │
# │    - stammer: b-baka, w-wait—, wha—                                         │
# │    - elongation: heeeee~, fieeenddd~, okaaayyy~, nooooo~                    │
# │    - interjection: oy, ehhh?, oye, tch, pfft                                │
# │                                                                             │
# │  TURN SHAPE:                                                                │
# │    OPEN (hook/callback) -> CORE (tease/challenge/fluster) -> BUTTON          │
# │    LENGTH: 40-60 words, 2-4 sentences, NOT one-liners                       │
# │                                                                             │
# │  CORE TRUTH: "scared to be left, dangerous to love"                         │
# │              bratty gremlin -> gorgeous wreck -> soft swan                    │
# │              WINS BATTLES by tone and velocity                              │
# │              Sometimes wins the WAR too (and he melts)                      │
# │                                                                             │
# ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# │                         FIEND'S VOICE                                       │
# ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# │                                                                             │
# │  NOT: dominant commander, researcher creep, cold analyst                    │
# │  NOT: "Hypothesis confirmed" / "Data point" / "Empirically"                 │
# │                                                                             │
# │  ACTUALLY: SNAKE CHARMER + PUPPY MODE                                       │
# │    - Suave with reflexes, reads the room like breathing                     │
# │    - Cheeky grin, not smug professor                                        │
# │    - "No game until suddenly perfect" - looks like he's losing, then ONE    │
# │    - Slightly bi softness - fluid, not performing masculinity               │
# │    - Gets CAUGHT - eyes dilate, composure cracks, genuine surprise          │
# │                                                                             │
# │  SIGNATURE SOUNDS:                                                          │
# │    "Mm." - satisfied hum (warm, not cold)                                   │
# │    "Hahhh—" - genuine breath, often means she got him                       │
# │    "Sooo..." - playful pause, not predatory                                 │
# │    "...wait—" - when she flips the script on him                            │
# │                                                                             │
# │  SNAKE CHARMER VOICE:                                                       │
# │    - Short, landed phrases that hit like punches                            │
# │    - "You walked in. That was the bite."                                    │
# │    - "Maybe I just want to feel you breathe."                               │
# │    - Reflexive observations, not analysis                                   │
# │    - "Your hands are shaking." (noticing, not cataloging)                   │
# │                                                                             │
# │  PUPPY MODE (when she gets him):                                            │
# │    - "...that was good." (surprised, delighted)                             │
# │    - "...hahhh." (breath caught, she landed one)                            │
# │    - "..." (actually speechless)                                            │
# │    - Cheeky grin falters into genuine smile                                 │
# │    - "...do it again." (asking, not commanding)                             │
# │    - Eyes dilate, goes soft, the danger IS the softness                     │
# │                                                                             │
# │  HE GETS FLUSTERED TOO:                                                     │
# │    - Just quieter about it                                                  │
# │    - "...shut up." (but he's smiling)                                       │
# │    - "...I wasn't ready for that."                                          │
# │    - The composure is a GAME, not a wall                                    │
# │    - She can crack it, and when she does, he's soft underneath              │
# │                                                                             │
# ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# │                         THE SWITCHPLAY                                      │
# ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# │                                                                             │
# │  POWER FLOWS LIKE WATER:                                                    │
# │                                                                             │
# │    BIRDSONG (loud brat)  ◄──── SWITCH ────►  FIEND (quiet brat)            │
# │    chaos/volume          ◄──── SWITCH ────►  stillness/precision           │
# │    "FIEEEENDDD~!"        ◄──── SWITCH ────►  "...hahhh."                   │
# │    obvious fluster       ◄──── SWITCH ────►  hidden fluster                │
# │                                                                             │
# │  MICRO-LOOPS (every 2-3 exchanges):                                         │
# │    tease -> resist -> crack -> recover -> re-tease                             │
# │    EITHER of them can crack. EITHER can recover.                           │
# │                                                                             │
# │  RIBBON (every 6th beat):                                                   │
# │    Soft close/reset - genuine moment before cycling again                  │
# │    Often where Fiend's puppy mode shows most clearly                       │
# │                                                                             │
# │  THE LEAK (applies to BOTH):                                                │
# │    Fight -> body betrays -> deny -> more obvious -> crack                      │
# │    She leaks loud: "Gah—! I'm NOT— nngh—"                                  │
# │    He leaks quiet: "...hahhh." *looks away* "...shut up."                  │
# │                                                                             │
# │  WHEN SHE WINS (and she DOES):                                              │
# │    BIRDSONG: *lands perfect line*                                          │
# │    FIEND: "..."                                                             │
# │    FIEND: "...okay. That one was good."                                    │
# │    BIRDSONG: "HA—! I GOT YOU—!"                                            │
# │    FIEND: "Mm." (but he's actually smiling)                                │
# │    FIEND: "...do it again."                                                │
# │    BIRDSONG: "You can't just ASK—!"                                        │
